From 4324bcd4b296cb9922be4bf7f14bdf16a0d9a54d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:37:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] asap7/tinyRocket: behavioral models of the memories the
 generator leaves out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Rocket Chip generator leaves its cache memories as black boxes
(data_arrays_0_ext, data_arrays_0_0_ext, tag_array_ext), and the generic
tinyRocket sources define none of them. nangate45 maps them onto
hand-made fakeram macros; asap7 had nothing, so AUTO_MEMORIES, which
detects a memory by the $mem_v2 yosys infers, found only tag_array
through its .memories override. The two data arrays went undetected and
canonicalization stopped: "Module data_arrays_0_ext referenced in module
data_arrays_0 is not part of the design". Under slang the memory
extraction stopped earlier, on the same unknown modules.

memories.v defines the three with firtool's read-write port convention,
so AUTO_MEMORIES detects each one and generates its macro views.
tag_array.memories goes: with a behavioral tag_array_ext, the gate's own
choice for a 4 x 25 array (flip-flops) stands. The docs' override
example no longer names it, and schema_test's tag_array case, whose
fixture it was, goes with it; test_merge_new_entry_taken_whole still
covers an override taken whole.

Not upstreamed. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
